// v1.0.16068 (per Mike, 8/21/26): CONFIRMED root cause of the "2-3 second delay, scales with
// result count" issue — Playlist Cheat's result rows were plain inline JSX inside a bare .map(),
// with zero memoization. CrateRow/CrateList above ARE memoized, which is exactly why Crate Cheat
// doesn't have this problem at any result count. The mechanism: this whole app is one giant
// component, so ANY state change anywhere (including totally unrelated background ticks, like the
// Artist Era Resolver's periodic progress updates) re-renders the entire thing. A memoized child
// with STABLE props (matching by shallow prop comparison) can bail out of that re-render entirely;
// an unmemoized inline .map() cannot — it regenerates every row's JSX from scratch on every single
